<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 3.994 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 3.994 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.994 billion pesos from the secondary market Wednesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    150 million    337 days</p>
<p>    150 million    175 days</p>
<p>    150 million     85 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    660 million     50 days</p>
<p>    660 million     43 days</p>
<p>    680 million     30 days</p>
<p>    700 million     29 days</p>
<p>    700 million     20 days</p>
<p>    144 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
